Understanding EDT Lessons in Finglas
Essential Driver Training, or EDT, is an organized training program for trainee automobile drivers in Ireland.

The usual curriculum is 12 x 1-hour sessions with an approved driving instructor. Eligible drivers may qualify for a discounted EDT, which consists of six sessions under the applicable RSA requirements.

For the latest updates, read the official RSA guide to Essential Driver Training.

The 12 lessons of EDT include:

The EDT curriculum gradually builds basic driving abilities. Topics covered include vehicle control, changing direction, observation, anticipation, sharing the road, speed management, and driving in various situations.

Instead of treating each class as a standalone assignment, learners should use the feedback from past sessions to enhance their performance in future sessions.

For example, if you find it difficult to observe around roundabouts, your teacher can help you build a routine for observing traffic, estimating gaps, choosing the right lane, and reacting safely.

Learners must also ensure completed sessions appear in their MyEDT records. When preparing for the driving exam, missing or incorrect records can pose complications.

